            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0037" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation (3)A/319: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Uruguay</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dwyer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-16T17:00:00-04:00">June 16, 1943—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. For Spaeth from Duggan. Your 573 June 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d23-f1"/> While the Department perceives no objection to
                    negotiations to secure Chilean approval of the proposed report concerning
                    Committee membership, it is inclined to believe that the formal adoption or
                    issuance of report should be withheld long enough to ascertain whether Argentina
                    intends to sever relations within a reasonable time. Please report views of
                    Guani and yourself. [Duggan.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
